message: "Please cite the accompanying paper and identify the commit used."
type: software
title: "Nonhalting and PA-independence for a 196-state Turing machine"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chang"
    given-names: "James"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jamesyc/BusyBeaver"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An explicit 196-state binary Turing machine runs forever from a blank tape.
  Ordinary Peano arithmetic proves neither its exact arithmetic halting
  sentence nor its negation. The machine and both conclusions are formalized
  in Lean 4.
